{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrym2cYkPz51odgt86WS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, with the sync wrapper, and all 10 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest tests`, Python 3.14, pytest 9.1.1). I haven't committed anything.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**: `get`, `close`, `__aenter__` and `__aexit__` are async. The default transport uses `asyncio.sleep(0.01)` and still raises `KeyError` for `/404` URLs. Retries use `asyncio.sleep` with the same doubling backoff, and only `TransientError` is retried.\n- **`get_many`**: uses `asyncio.gather` behind an `asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrency)`, so results keep input order. Per-URL exceptions come back as `FetchError` in the list and are not raised.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is async and returns the same dict shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs the client under `asyncio.run` and returns the `get_many` list, with `bytes` or `FetchError` entries.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**: the three original tests are ported to `asyncio.run`, so no pytest-asyncio dependency is added. New tests cover:\n  - retries running out raises `TransientError`\n  - non-transient errors are not retried\n  - the concurrency limit is respected and order is kept\n  - `close()` blocks further `get` calls\n  - `fetch_all` with an injected transport and with the default transport\n\n**Decisions I made that you didn't specify**\n\n- `Client` rejects `max_concurrency < 1` with `ValueError`. A zero-sized semaphore would deadlock.\n- The semaphore is created per `get_many` call rather than in `__init__`, so a client can be reused across separate `asyncio.run` calls.\n- `fetcher/__init__.py` is unchanged, so callers import the wrapper as `from fetcher.sync import fetch_all`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8523,"cache_read_input_tokens":49580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8523},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20fe3eee-5987-4d1e-96a1-10fcaf4c2113","uuid":"cf4e6825-dcf2-434f-a9f5-1a7569ea2446","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:28:56.050Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrym2Lvq9wqZp5mENFQm"}
